# ADE architecture

GOAL -> UNDERSTAND -> PLAN -> RESEARCH -> ARCHITECT -> IMPLEMENT -> TEST -> REVIEW -> SECURITY -> OPTIMIZE -> RELEASE -> OBSERVE.
Only the stages the goal needs are run.

- For any non-trivial goal, start with the `orchestrator` skill (`.cursor/skills/orchestrator/SKILL.md`). It picks the route.
- Rules = permanent policy (`.cursor/rules`). Skills = reusable procedures (`.cursor/skills`). Subagents = isolated
  specialists (`.cursor/agents`). Use a subagent for research, independent review, or parallelizable work; otherwise stay in the main context.
- Contracts and diagrams: `docs/framework/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `WORKFLOW.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `SKILLS.md`, `GOVERNANCE.md`.
- Resume before acting: read `docs/framework/SESSION.md` first when starting a session; it says what state the framework is in and what is pending.
- Analyze before modifying: read `docs/framework/REPOSITORY_ANALYSIS.md` and the code you will touch. Reuse existing code and config.
- No new dependency or infrastructure the project does not need. Significant decisions -> ADR in `docs/framework/adr/`.
- Spec-driven features may use Spec Kit (`/speckit-specify`, `-plan`, `-tasks`, `-implement`); principles in `.specify/memory/constitution.md`.

## Human authority (never bypass)

Ask for explicit approval before: production actions, destructive operations (data, files, git history), mass changes
(more than ~10 files or cross-cutting refactors), high-impact architecture changes, secret or permission changes,
irreversible actions. `scripts/ade/guard.py` (hook) enforces part of this at shell level; it is a backstop, not a substitute for judgment.

## Definition of Done (report every item: PASS / FAIL / N/A with evidence)

[ ] Code implemented [ ] Build OK [ ] New tests [ ] Existing tests pass [ ] No known regressions
[ ] Lint passes [ ] Type check passes (if applicable) [ ] Code review done [ ] Security review done
[ ] Docs updated (if applicable) [ ] Git diff reviewed [ ] Acceptance criteria met

Never say "done" because code was written. Run `python scripts/ade/verify.py` for the mechanical items.
